# ---- fleet registry read path (optional, BH-5649) ----
# Where bin/fleet-conf.sh and bin/render-cron.sh read the project, box and lane
# membership registry. file (the default) reads the committed fleet.conf and
# catalog/lanes.d. db reads harness-jobs GET /api/registry first, then the last
# good cache in state/registry/, then the committed files; an outage writes one
# ALERTS line and never stops a cron or a build. bin/harness-sync.sh appends
# REGISTRY_SOURCE=db here once, when this file has no REGISTRY_SOURCE= line and
# the registry answers with the checkout's projects (BH-5651). The code default
# stays file. Set REGISTRY_SOURCE=file to keep a box on the committed files:
# the seed never overwrites an existing line.
#REGISTRY_SOURCE=file
# Seconds a cached registry answers with no HTTP call (db mode only). 0 asks
# the worker on every call.
#REGISTRY_CACHE_TTL_S=60
# Seconds one GET /api/registry may take before the cache answers instead.
#REGISTRY_API_TIMEOUT_S=5
# REGISTRY_ADMIN_TOKEN is a SECRET, not a knob: the worker secret that gates
# POST /api/registry/import (`npx wrangler secret put REGISTRY_ADMIN_TOKEN` in
# worker/jobs) and the same value in the operator env that runs
# bin/registry-seed.sh. Never put its value in this file.
